
#   UULIB:Domain    Domain data base for mailer
#
#   Refer to MAN:Domains for information on how the domain file works
#   This file holds domain information for properly routing email when
#   you talk to several adjacent sites.  When you can talk to just a
#   single site this file should contain a single master default to
#   that site.
#
#   SAMPLE MULTI-SITE DOMAIN FILE, commented out.  If your UUCP
#   site connects to only one other site you do not need a Domain
#   file, simply set the 'DefaultNode' entry in UULIB:Config to
#   that site.
#
#   If you can talk UUCP to multiple other sites and wish to route
#   various domains to different sites you need to construct a Domain
#   file that looks something like that below.  The first entry, '*',
#   serves as a default and you do not need a 'DefaultNode' entry
#   in UULIB:Config.
#
#   Again, refer to the manual pages.
#
#*               MF UU   sorinc.UUCP
#*.EDU           MF UU   fubar.UUCP!buggy.CTS.COM
#*.COM           MF UU   chugly.UUCP

*                MF UU   crash.UUCP
cnet577          MD UU   cnet577.UUCP
cnet577.cts.com  MD UU   cnet577.UUCP
centaur          MD UU   centaur.UUCP
